/S /H1
/T (The pending property is used to disable the submit button while the form is in the middle of submission. When pending is true, it shows a loading message, providing feedback to the user that the form is being processed. Once the form has submitted successfully, data will hold any response information returned from the submission. Here, if data is populated \(e.g., it has a username field\), we display a welcome message to the user. method and action provide useful metadata about the form. In this example, they are shown as debugging information to indicate the HTTP method and action URL being used. )
/E (The pending property is used to disable the submit button while the form is in the middle of submission. When pending is true, it shows a loading message, providing feedback to the user that the form is being processed. Once the form has submitted successfully, data will hold any response information returned from the submission. Here, if data is populated \(e.g., it has a username field\), we display a welcome message to the user. method and action provide useful metadata about the form. In this example, they are shown as debugging information to indicate the HTTP method and action URL being used. )
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [1]
